    {
      "id": "p65h7lo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Composition of High Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0g28hne",
      "content": "• A High Court consists of a Chief Justice and other judges."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r5yud6y",
      "content": "• The number of judges is decided by the President depending on workload."
    },
    {
      "id": "6qsog0x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Appointment of High Court Judges"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yhnmzi9",
      "content": "• Judges are appointed by the President of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qe3wvk8",
      "content": "• Consultation with Chief Justice of India, Governor, and Chief Justice of High Court."
    },
    {
      "id": "bnwg04k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Qualifications of High Court Judges"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0y154rt",
      "content": "• Citizen of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g2y43dp",
      "content": "• 10 years judicial office OR 10 years advocate in High Court."
    },
    {
      "id": "j1km406",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Tenure"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xh5a0nq",
      "content": "• Judges retire at age 62."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mv4qr5q",
      "content": "• They can resign to the President."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lzy2dg7",
      "content": "• They can be removed through impeachment."
    },
    {
      "id": "gctg5ew",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Jurisdiction of High Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4v241oe",
      "content": "Original, Appellate, Writ, and Supervisory jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "id": "xujnww2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Types of Writs"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The writ jurisdiction of the High Court under Article 226 is wider than that of the Supreme Court under Article 32.",
        "High Court judges are appointed and removed by the President, even though they take their oath before the State Governor.",
        "Parliament holds the exclusive power to extend or exclude the jurisdiction of a High Court to/from any Union Territory."
      ],
      "id": "cn8ywcx"
    },
